<title>JAPAN: Japan May rubber imports down 5.3 pct yr/yr-MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan May rubber imports down 5.3 pct yr/yr-MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's rubber imports in May totalled 47,191 tonnes, down by 5.3 percent from a year earlier, Finance Ministry data released on Friday showed.</p>
<p>Figures were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			May 97	 Apr 97	May 96</p>
<p> Total		47,191	 54,287	49,845</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Thailand	   36,162	 42,286	37,087</p>
<p> Indonesia	   8,721	  9,138	 9,853</p>
<p> Malaysia	    1,250	  2,160	 1,803</p>
<p>Total imports in the first five months of calendar 1997 were 305,377 tonnes against 291,089 tonnes in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk (+81-3-3432-7391)</p>
</text>
